Let me write fd.py first. Key design: derivative operators as matrices or as functions using np.roll? For convergence tests, dense matrices are fine and exact. For time evolution, matrix-vector multiply is fine for N up to ~2000. Use dense 1D matrices.

Periodic operators:
- D1 order 2: (u[i+1]-u[i-1])/(2h)
- D1 order 4: (-u[i+2]+8u[i+1]-8u[i-1]+u[i-2])/(12h)
- D1 order 6: (u[i+3]-9u[i+2]+45u[i+1]-45u[i-1]+9u[i-2]-u[i-3])/(60h)
- D2 order 2: (u[i+1]-2u[i]+u[i-1])/h²
