## N0 flat-space scalar-wave calibration — delivered

**Scope discipline held:** flat-space massless scalar only; no self-gravitating solver code exists (`numerics/spherical_solver/` absent); N1 is machine-locked.

### Results — three independent discretisations agree

| implementation | method | primary order | gates |
|---|---|---:|---|
| `numerics/tests/flat_wave.py` (worker 12, rev `8b52014d`) | MOL RK4, `v = r·u`, central FD 2/4 | **2.0000** | 11/11 |
| `numerics/tests/flat_wave_replication.py` (worker 13, rev `8ade1cdc`) | implicit Crank–Nicolson + FD, and CN + P1 FEM | **1.9935 / 1.9863** | verdict ORDER REPRODUCED |
| `numerics/tests/lead_calibration.py` (lead, rev `dc369e3d`) | staggered finite-volume **SBP** + Cartesian 2/4/6 | **2.0006** | 10/10 |

Max disagreement **0.0101** (tolerance 0.35). Invariants: SBP energy identity residual **7e-18**, constraint <1e-13, flux-closure order **2.00**, dispersion symbol match **4e-16**, U(1) charge drift 1.5e-13. All negative controls (frozen, wrong-sign, CFL=1.5) rejected; the non-SBP collocated control is rejected by >1e15×.

### Defects found and fixed (calibration caught its own errors)
